accessibility	Tag: no-alt-text, descriptive-link-text
atx	Tag: no-missing-space-atx, no-multiple-space-atx
atx_closed	Tag: no-missing-space-closed-atx, no-multiple-space-closed-atx
blank_lines	Tag: no-multiple-blank-lines, heading-blank-lines, blanks-around-fences, blanks-around-lists, single-trailing-newline
blanks-around-fences	Fenced code blocks have a blank or comment line above and below.
blanks-around-lists	Lists outside other lists have a blank or comment line above and below.
blanks-around-tables	Tables have a blank or comment line above and below.
blockquote	Tag: no-multiple-space-blockquote, no-blanks-blockquote
bullet	Tag: unordered-list-style, list-indent, ul-indent, blanks-around-lists
code	Tag: commands-show-output, blanks-around-fences, no-space-in-code, fenced-code-language, code-block-style, code-fence-style
code-block-style	Code blocks all use the first block's style, fenced or indented.
code-fence-style	Code fences all use the first fence's character, backtick or tilde.
commands-show-output	Code blocks that show only commands leave out the $ prompt.
descriptive-link-text	Link text describes its target instead of saying "click here" or "more".
emphasis	Tag: no-emphasis-as-heading, no-space-in-emphasis, emphasis-style, strong-style
emphasis-style	All italic text uses one marker, *text* or _text_, except * inside a word.
fenced-code-language	Fenced code blocks name their language after the opening fence.
first-line-heading	Comments aside, the file starts with a top-level heading or front matter title.
hard_tab	Tag: no-hard-tabs
heading-blank-lines	Headings have a blank or comment line above and below.
heading-increment	Each heading is at most one level deeper than the heading or title before it.
heading-start-left	Headings start at the beginning of their line, list item or blockquote.
heading-style	Headings all use the first heading's style: # Title, # Title #, or underlined.
headings	Tag: heading-increment, heading-style, no-missing-space-atx, no-multiple-space-atx, no-missing-space-closed-atx, no-multiple-space-closed-atx, heading-blank-lines, heading-start-left, no-duplicate-heading, single-h1, no-trailing-punctuation, no-emphasis-as-heading, first-line-heading, required-headings
hr	Tag: hr-style
hr-style	Every horizontal rule is written the same way as the first one, such as ---.
html	Tag: no-inline-html
images	Tag: no-alt-text, reference-links-images, link-image-reference-definitions, link-image-style
indentation	Tag: list-indent, ul-indent, no-multiple-space-blockquote
language	Tag: fenced-code-language
line-length	Lines fit in 80 characters, with exemptions such as lone links and definitions.
line_length	Tag: line-length
link-destination-style	Relative links and local file: URLs are not mixed in one document.
link-fragments	Links to a #fragment point at a heading or anchor in the same file, or at #top.
link-image-reference-definitions	Every reference definition is used and defined once, except [//] comments.
link-image-style	Links and images use only the allowed styles. By default, all are allowed.
links	Tag: no-reversed-links, no-bare-urls, no-space-in-links, no-empty-links, link-fragments, reference-links-images, link-image-reference-definitions, link-image-style, descriptive-link-text, link-destination-style
list-indent	Items in a list start at the same column. Ordered numbers may right-align.
list-marker-space	One space, or one tab, separates each list marker from the item's text.
no-alt-text	Markdown images have alt text, and HTML images have alt or aria-hidden="true".
no-bare-urls	Outside code and HTML, URLs and email addresses sit in angle brackets or links.
no-blanks-blockquote	No blank line sits between two blockquotes.
no-duplicate-heading	No two headings have exactly the same text.
no-emphasis-as-heading	Outside lists and blockquotes, a bold or italic line is not a stand-in heading.
no-empty-links	Inline links have a destination, and no link points at just #.
no-hard-tabs	Lines contain no tab characters, including inside code.
no-inline-html	Documents contain no raw HTML elements other than allowed ones.
no-missing-space-atx	A space follows the # marks that open a heading at the start of a line.
no-missing-space-closed-atx	A closed heading at the start of a line has a space inside each run of #.
no-multiple-blank-lines	Outside code, no two blank lines follow each other, except after front matter.
no-multiple-space-atx	Only one space follows the # marks that open a heading.
no-multiple-space-blockquote	Outside code and list item text, at most one space follows a blockquote's >.
no-multiple-space-closed-atx	A closed heading has only one space inside each run of #.
no-reversed-links	Inline links put the text in brackets and the URL in parentheses: [text](url).
no-space-in-code	Code span text has no spaces around it, except one each side or by a backtick.
no-space-in-emphasis	Emphasis markers touch the text they wrap, as in **bold**.
no-space-in-links	Link text has no spaces just inside its brackets.
no-trailing-punctuation	Headings do not end with a period, comma, semicolon, colon or exclamation mark.
no-trailing-spaces	Outside code blocks, lines end in no spaces or tabs, or in exactly 2 of them.
ol	Tag: ol-prefix, list-marker-space, blanks-around-lists
ol-prefix	Ordered list items are numbered 1, 1, 1, or 1, 2, 3, or 0, 1, 2, and so on.
proper-names	Outside URLs, proper names match the configured capitals, none by default.
reference-links-images	Labels in [text][label] and [label][] references are defined, except x.
required-headings	Headings follow the configured outline in order. No outline is set by default.
single-h1	A document that starts with a title has no other top-level heading.
single-trailing-newline	The file ends with a newline, or a last line of only whitespace, > or comments.
spaces	Tag: no-missing-space-atx, no-multiple-space-atx, no-missing-space-closed-atx, no-multiple-space-closed-atx, heading-start-left
spelling	Tag: proper-names
strong-style	All bold text uses one marker, **text** or __text__, except ** inside a word.
table	Tag: table-pipe-style, table-column-count, blanks-around-tables, table-column-style, table-alignment
table-alignment	Each cell of a table's delimiter row has at least 3 dashes.
table-column-count	Every table row has as many cells as the header row.
table-column-style	Each table follows one style: aligned pipes, one space of padding, or none.
table-pipe-style	Table rows use leading and trailing pipes the same way throughout.
ul	Tag: unordered-list-style, list-indent, ul-indent, list-marker-space, blanks-around-lists
ul-indent	Outside ordered lists, bullets sit at the margin and indent 2 spaces per level.
unordered-list-style	Every bullet uses the same marker as the first bullet in the file.
url	Tag: no-bare-urls, link-destination-style
whitespace	Tag: no-trailing-spaces, no-hard-tabs, no-multiple-blank-lines, no-multiple-space-blockquote, no-blanks-blockquote, list-marker-space, no-space-in-emphasis, no-space-in-code, no-space-in-links
:4
